{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"review-plan round 1: BLOCK (1 blocking, 10 advisory). Blocking finding: the plan named PROXY_IDENTITY as the principal seam, which exists only under the proxy strategy; PAT/JWKS paths carry the principal inside the SDK AccessToken. Remediated: principal now comes from mcp.server.auth.middleware.auth_context.get_access_token().client_id (AuthContextMiddleware is installed by FastMCP.streamable_http_app whenever a token verifier is configured; every rebar verifier returns AccessToken(client_id=...)); the hint middleware is wired unconditionally (not proxy-gated); resolver consumers enumerated (txn, cross_session, session_log pointer rotation, transition_close audit string, _llm_commands CLI-only); client recipes narrowed to the three supported clients (Codex env_http_headers verified against the current config reference; Copilot principal-only); the contract test drives the real ASGI app via httpx.ASGITransport so both middlewares run; docs ACs and rollout/rollback added. Re-running review-plan."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788562675502133001,"uuid":"51eafe47-d5d9-46c2-86bc-98ba1557c319"}